  - sim/sweep_eval.py           derived from source/sim_to_real_so101/scripts/lerobot_eval.py
  - docker/sim/Dockerfile       the course's docker/sim/Dockerfile with two pinned dependencies (see Dockerfile.diff)
  - docker/sim/entrypoint_offline.sh  the course's docker/sim/entrypoint.sh without the runtime pip install
                                      (see entrypoint_offline.diff)
  - assets/local/*.local.usda   wrapper layers that sublayer the course's unmodified USD files
  - explore/sweep_eval_long.py  derived from the same lerobot_eval.py, through sim/sweep_eval.py
  - sim/trace_episode.py, sim/render_poses.py, sim/jaw_tips.py
                                derived from the same lerobot_eval.py, through sim/sweep_eval.py
  - e3/cache/scene.npz          triangles from the course's USD files mat.usda and Vial_rack_simple.usda, and box
                                panels from the bounding boxes of lightbox-simple.usd (written by e3/render.py)
  - stencils/*.pdf              vial outlines projected from the course's Vial_opaque.usda (tools/make_stencils.py)
  - results/c1/, results/overlay_refs/
                                renders of the course's simulated scene (front and wrist cameras at the nominal
                                pose, front camera at the R0 pose), their instance masks, and the scene's pose
                                dump (sim/dump_scene.py)
The derived Python files (sim/sweep_eval.py, explore/sweep_eval_long.py, sim/trace_episode.py, sim/render_poses.py,
sim/jaw_tips.py) keep NVIDIA's copyright and license header.
The rest of the code imports the course's modules and Isaac-GR00T at run time; neither is included here.
